<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=wohler-synthesis">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Chemistry</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wöhler synthesis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Wohler synthesis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wöhler synthesis is the conversion of ammonium cyanate into urea, described by Friedrich Wöhler in 1828 and often cited as the starting point of modern organic chemistry. Wöhler made urea from several sets of reactants, such as cyanic acid with ammonia. That it brought down vitalism, the theory that organic matter possessed a &quot;vital force&quot;, is disputed: the work of John Dalton and Jöns Jacob Berzelius had already convinced chemists that organic and inorganic matter obey the same chemical laws, and vitalism began to lose support only after 1845.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wohler-synthesis.jpg" alt="Wöhler synthesis" width="320" height="359" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rudolph Hoffmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_W%C3%B6hler_Litho.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1828</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Friedrich Wöhler</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Whether it overthrew vitalism, the source of its fame, is disputed.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/chemical-revolution">Modern chemistry<span>1787</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/aspirin">Aspirin<span>1853</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/bakelite">Plastics<span>1907</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=wohler-synthesis">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
